We propose six experimental phases, now incorporating calibration requirements, scale-robustness testing, and the statistics-structure dissociation.

Phase I: Replication with Calibration

Replicate existing cross-model representation studies across scientific domains, applying null-calibration to distinguish genuine convergence from scale artifacts.

Phase II: Independence

Construct training regimes minimizing dataset and preprocessing overlap, with explicit control of input statistics.

